</div><h3>Layer 2: Protective Wrapping</h3><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Prevents surface scratches and minor abrasions during handling.</p><ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Material: Soft, anti‑static polyethylene (PE) wrap or microfiber cloths.</span></li><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Technique: Overlap each wrap segment by 25 % and secure with low‑adhesive tape to avoid residue.</span></li></ul><h3>Layer 3: Frame Padding</h3><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Cushions the bike’s frame against impact and vibration.</p><ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Material: High‑density foam panels (1‑2 cm thick) covered with a tear‑resistant nylon sleeve.</span></li><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Technique: Cut foam to match tube geometry, then wrap with the nylon sleeve and secure with zip ties.</span></li></ul><h3>Layer 4: Component Isolation</h3><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Separates delicate components (e.g., handlebars, seat post, wheels) to avoid contact damage.</p><ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Material: Bubble‑wrap or recyclable corrugated cardboard inserts.</span></li><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Technique: Individually wrap each component, then place within molded cardboard trays that lock together.</span></li></ul><h3>Layer 5: Crate or Box Enclosure</h3><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Provides a rigid outer shell that distributes loads evenly.</p><ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Material: Double‑wall corrugated cardboard boxes or lightweight aluminum frames with interior wood panels.</span></li><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Technique: Assemble the crate with reinforced corner brackets; line interior walls with additional foam strips.</span></li></ul><h3>Layer 6: Securing &amp; Bracing</h3><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Immobilizes the bike within the transport vehicle to prevent movement.</p><ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Material: Ratchet straps, non‑slip rubber mats, and adjustable tie‑down anchors.</span></li><li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Technique: Po